# DesignTokens Migration Guide

> Full migration tracker: `documents/DesignSystem_Migration_Plan.md`
> Token definitions: `step/Config/DesignTokens.swift`

## Before You Start

1. Read `step/Config/DesignTokens.swift` to see all available tokens
2. Only migrate values that **exactly match** a token — don't force mismatches
3. Do NOT change colors, logic, behavior, or view structure
4. Do NOT fix lint errors unless explicitly asked

## Typography Migration

| Before | After |
|---|---|
| `.scaledFont(size: 34, weight: .bold, design: .rounded)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.display)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 34, weight: .bold, design: .monospaced)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.displayMono)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 28, weight: .semibold, design: .rounded)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.heading)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 24, weight: .semibold, design: .rounded)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.title)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 20, weight: .medium)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.titleSmall)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 18, weight: .semibold)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.bodyLarge)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 16, weight: .regular)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.body)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 16, weight: .medium)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.bodyMedium)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 17, weight: .semibold)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.buttonLabel)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 15, weight: .medium)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.label)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 14, weight: .regular)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.bodySmall)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 14, weight: .medium)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.bodySmallMedium)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 13, weight: .regular)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.caption)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 12, weight: .regular)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.captionSmall)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 11, weight: .medium)` + `.tracking(1.0)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.overline)` |
| `.scaledFont(size: 10, weight: .medium)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.micro)` |
| `.textStyle(.spotlightTitle)` | `.scaledFont(DesignTokens.Typography.title)` |
| `.font(.system(size: N, weight: W))` | `.scaledFont(size: N, weight: W)` or matching token |

When using a token, **remove** any separate `.tracking(...)` modifier — tokens apply tracking automatically.

## Spacing & Layout Migration

| Before | After |
|---|---|
| `.padding(.horizontal, 20)` (page edges) | `.padding(.horizontal, DesignTokens.Layout.pageMargin)` |
| `.padding(.bottom, 120)` (floating CTA) | `.padding(.bottom, DesignTokens.Layout.bottomSafeArea)` |
| Vertical spacing `32` between sections | `DesignTokens.Layout.sectionSpacing` |
| Card spacing `12` | `DesignTokens.Layout.cardSpacing` |
| Header bottom spacing `24` | `DesignTokens.Layout.headerBottom` |
| Other: `2, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32` | `DesignTokens.Spacing.xxs/xs/sm/md/base/lg/xl/xxl` |

## Contextual Spacing Guide

When choosing a spacing token, **consider the context** — not just the numeric value. Each token has a semantic purpose:

| Token | Value | Semantic Use |
|---|---|---|
| `xxs` (2pt) | Hairline separators, border offsets, fine-tuning only |
| `xs` (4pt) | Minimal gaps — inline icon-to-text in the same line, pill padding |
| `sm` (8pt) | Tight spacing — icon-to-title inside cards, label-to-sublabel |
| `md` (12pt) | Card internal gaps — between distinct content blocks inside a card |
| `base` (16pt) | Card content padding, standard internal padding |
| `lg` (20pt) | Page margins, generous separation |
| `xl` (24pt) | Header spacing, large visual breaks |
| `xxl` (32pt) | Major section spacing |

### Card Internal Rhythm

Inside a card, use spacing that creates readable visual hierarchy:

| Relationship | Recommended Token |
|---|---|
| Icon → Title | `sm` (8pt) or `md` (12pt) |
| Title → Subtitle / Description | `xs` (4pt) or `sm` (8pt) |
| Content block → Action button | `md` (12pt) or `base` (16pt) |
| Card content padding (`.padding()`) | `base` (16pt) |

**Never** use `xxs` for spacing between an icon and a title — it produces a cramped, unreadable layout. Reserve `xxs` for hairline gaps only.

**Never** use arithmetic on tokens (e.g. `xxs + 1`, `base - 2`). If no token matches exactly, leave the raw value and add a `// Figma: Npx` comment.

